{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime.\n\n```rust,ignore\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    type Error: Send;\n    type NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync;\n    type NodeContent: NodeContents;\n    type EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync;\n\n    fn cache(&self) -> &ValidationCache;\n    fn node_path(&self, node: &Self::NodeId) -> NodePath;\n    fn node_content(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n    ) -> Result<Self::NodeContent, Self::Error>;\n    fn outgoing_edges(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        label: Self::EdgeLabel,\n    ) -> Result<Vec<Self::NodeId>, Self::Error>;\n    fn load_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<Option<Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>>, Self::Error>> + Send;\n    fn store_evidence(\n        &self,\n        node: &Self::NodeId,\n        criterion: &CriterionPath,\n        record: &Record<Self::NodeId, Self::EdgeLabel>,\n    ) -> impl Future<Output = Result<(), Self::Error>> + Send;\n\n    fn project_sources(&self) -> Option<SourceProject<Self>> { ... }\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Verdict:** the reviewed tests adequately check `requirements.sdk.domain`.\n\n**Obligations in the text**\n- The trait is `Domain: Clone + Send + Sync`.\n- The associated types have these bounds:\n  - `Error: Send`\n  - `NodeId: Clone + Eq + Send + Sync`\n  - `NodeContent: NodeContents`\n  - `EdgeLabel: Clone + Send + Sync`\n- The trait has these methods: `cache`, `node_path`, `node_content`, `outgoing_edges`, `load_evidence` and `store_evidence`.\n- The `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` futures are `Send`.\n- `project_sources` has the stated signature.\n- A domain is cloneable and safe to share between executions.\n\n**Mapping to tests**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` implements `Domain` for a fixture. The fixture's identity, label and error types are deliberately minimal:\n  - `Identity` has no Debug or Hash.\n  - `Label` has no Eq.\n  - `GraphError` is not Sync, Debug, Clone or Error.\n- The fixture implements every required method with the declared signatures. It is `Clone`.\n- The nested `check_bounds::<G: Domain>` function compiles generic code against the declared bounds. It requires `Clone + Send + Sync` for the domain, the identity bounds, the label bounds and `Send` for the error. It also requires that the futures returned by `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` are `Send`.\n- A loosened bound would fail to compile. An added bound would fail on the opaque fixture. The `Send` futures are also exercised at runtime.\n- The same test checks the behaviour of `node_path`, `node_content` and `outgoing_edges`, including duplicates, empty results and the error path.\n- The concurrency tests cover \"safe to share between executions\":\n  - `agent/tests.rs#fn[concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads]`\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]`\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`\n  - `graph/validation_tests.rs#fn[shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls]`\n- Other marked tests use real domain implementations end to end, including storing and loading evidence and node content.\n- `project_sources` is shown in the trait text only as `{ ... }`. The default result `None` is specified by the sources requirement, not here. The signature is compile-checked by the fixtures that omit it and by the override in `agent/configured.rs`.\n\n**Limitations**\n- `NodeContent` is only required to be `NodeContents`. The test asks for slightly more (`Send + Sync`), which is stricter, not weaker.\n- Behaviour of each method beyond its signature belongs to other requirements, such as the graph-edges, node-path and evidence requirements. It is not assessed here.\n\nI found no gap and no acknowledgments were needed.",
